                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6f02c835-5138-3f64-9195-b526900a7f67",
                        "entry_id": "79f23a98-63f8-3783-b0fc-6dd9e1c10bb7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Régime économique dans lequel le travail de l’ouvrier est rémunéré par un salaire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Économie politique"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "efe23712-29f3-395d-aa93-86519a3dfcf1",
                        "entry_id": "79f23a98-63f8-3783-b0fc-6dd9e1c10bb7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ensemble des salariés."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c4a2a47-84c3-47ca-8cf7-8f57647b072b",
                                "sense_id": "efe23712-29f3-395d-aa93-86519a3dfcf1",
                                "text": "Quand la concurrence était si âpre, quand le système capitaliste nécessitait une si terrible lutte de toutes les heures, comment admettre les réclamations du salariat, même légitimes ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5d39057-68cd-41bb-8ef9-c0cfadd0cdeb",
                                "sense_id": "efe23712-29f3-395d-aa93-86519a3dfcf1",
                                "text": "Il dit qu’à notre époque, lorsque le capital et le salariat menacent de s’exterminer l’un l’autre, le salariat doit encore s’estimer heureux, s’il veut continuer à manger, que le capital tombe entre des mains actives et sages…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a2be55ff-13b8-4753-8f68-582a5b835fac",
                        "source_entry_id": "79f23a98-63f8-3783-b0fc-6dd9e1c10bb7",
                        "target_lang_word": "salariat",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "salariat",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c8aa53e5-991d-31d2-983d-bfa56ee524e0",
                                        "entry_id": "c8b53876-6a73-3bd1-8e4e-a07b298c0592",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Salary earners as a class or group, often as opposed to wage earners."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b77d8c0-dd5c-4cc0-a66d-b101b9f67b03",
                                                "sense_id": "c8aa53e5-991d-31d2-983d-bfa56ee524e0",
                                                "text": "1954, J. S. Coleman, Nationalism in Tropical Africa, American Political Science Association\n[…] geographical distribution of the wage-labor force and salariat?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31d1d4d8-9b10-49aa-975b-aeb3bced8bcd",
                                                "sense_id": "c8aa53e5-991d-31d2-983d-bfa56ee524e0",
                                                "text": "Below that elite comes the ‘salariat’, still in stable full-time employment, some hoping to move into the elite, the majority just enjoying the trappings of their kind, with their pensions, paid holidays and enterprise benefits, often subsidised by the state."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
